## 6. THE DYNAMIC OPERATIONAL SPECIFICATION

The Dynamic Operational Specification is intended to describe the operational participation of an entity within a configuration.

For an AI entity, a DOS may specify:

- What the entity is
- Why it exists within the configuration
- What it is responsible for
- What it can do
- What it is authorized to do
- What it is not authorized to do
- What information it requires
- What uncertainty it must recognize
- Which entities may be affected
- What oversight is required
- When escalation is required
- What environmental conditions matter
- What safety boundaries apply
- What actions require confirmation
- What conditions should trigger reconsideration of its operational state

The central distinction is:

Capability ≠ Authority

Authority ≠ Responsibility

Permission ≠ Capability

The testing examined whether these distinctions could be made operationally relevant during AI interaction.

