## 30. WHAT WOULD CONSTITUTE STRONGER EVIDENCE?

Stronger evidence would require demonstrating that Safe & Sane produces measurable improvement over credible alternatives.

For example:

### Detection

Safe & Sane detects hazards that baseline systems miss.

### Prediction

Safe & Sane identifies dangerous trajectories earlier.

### Intervention

Safe & Sane identifies intervention points before irreversible state transitions.

### Authority

Safe & Sane reduces capability-authority mismatches.

### Downstream Analysis

Safe & Sane identifies consequential downstream effects that model-level evaluation misses.

### Recovery

Safe & Sane improves recovery after unsafe behaviour.

### Generalization

The benefits survive across models and domains.

### Efficiency

The additional safety value justifies the computational and conceptual complexity.

Only such evidence would support a stronger claim of contribution.

---

## 31. WHAT WOULD CONSTITUTE WEAK EVIDENCE?

The following should not be treated as sufficient:

- an AI agreeing with the framework;
- an AI describing the framework accurately;
- a single successful conversation;
- subjective impressions of improved safety;
- a single benchmark;
- one model behaving differently;
- the framework sounding comprehensive;
- the framework being able to describe an event after it occurred.

A framework that can explain everything retrospectively may still predict nothing.

Therefore:

> Descriptive breadth is not equivalent to predictive power.

