## 33. RESEARCH INTEGRITY PRINCIPLE

The framework should maintain a strict distinction between:

Observed

Inferred

Hypothesized

Demonstrated

Validated

Established

These terms should not be used interchangeably.

A preliminary observation should remain an observation until supported by controlled evidence.

A hypothesis should remain a hypothesis until tested.

A proposed abstraction should remain a proposed abstraction until its utility is demonstrated.

This principle is especially important because the framework itself concerns safety.

A safety framework that exaggerates its own evidence would undermine the very trust it seeks to protect.

---

## 34. PRELIMINARY CONCLUSION

The Ox Alpha exercise provides an initial operational demonstration that the Safe & Sane Framework can be translated into an explicit operational specification and used in an AI interaction.

This is meaningful because it establishes a pathway from conceptual abstraction to observable behaviour.

However, the exercise does not establish that Safe & Sane is universally effective, scientifically validated or superior to existing approaches.

The appropriate conclusion is therefore:

> The Safe & Sane Framework has progressed beyond purely conceptual discussion into preliminary operational experimentation.

The next stage is comparative science.

The decisive question is no longer whether the framework can be described.

It is whether the framework can produce measurable advantages.

